.TH "BINDLE_URLDESC" "3" "@RELEASE_MONTH@" "@PACKAGE_NAME@" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
bindle_hash_keys, bindle_hash_skeys - Bindle Binary Tools hash table key routines

.SH LIBRARY
Bindle Binaries Tools (libbindle, -lbindle)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include\fR \fB<bindle.h>\fR
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_keys( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", bindle_berval_t *** " bvap " );"
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_skeys( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", char *** " keysp " );"
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBbindle_hash_keys\fR() retrieves the keys of the hash referenced by
\fIbh\fR.  The function allocates a \fBNULL\fR terminated array of key values
stored as \fBbindle_berval_t\fR members.  The result will be stored to
\fI*bvap\fR.  The array and values stored to \fI*bvap\fR must be freed either
manually or using \fBbindle_bvarray_free\fR().
.sp
The \fBbindle_hash_skeys\fR() retrieves the keys of the hash referenced by
\fIbh\fR.  The function allocates a \fBNULL\fR terminated array of key values.
The result will be stored to \fI*keysp\fR.  The array and values stored to
\fI*keysp\fR must be freed either manually or using \fBbindle_strsfree\fR().

.SH RETURN VALUES
The \fBbindle_hash_keys\fR() and \fBbindle_hash_skeys\fR() functions return 0
if successful. If an error was encountered, \fIerrno\fR will be set and the
functions will return -1.
.sp
The result of \fBbindle_hash_keys\fR() must be
freed manually or using \fBbindle_bvarray_free\fR().  The result of
\fBbindle_hash_skeys\fR() must be freed manually or using
\fBbindle_strsfree\fR().

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bindletools (3),
.BR bindle_hash_initialize (3),
.BR bindle_hash_del (3),
.BR bindle_hash_get (3),
.BR bindle_hash_set (3),
.BR bindle_berval (3),
.BR bindle_hash_funcs (3)

.SH AUTHOR
David M. Syzdek <david@syzdek.net>

